From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:51:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: clear the hibernation marker when the PM notifier
 fails

Found auditing the hibernation thaw and poweroff patch: if this notifier fails
PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE, the kernel doesn't call it for PM_POST_HIBERNATION, so
nv_hibernation_in_progress stayed set and the next normal shutdown or reboot would skip
the driver teardown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
index c336288d..1d797617 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv.c
@@ -4809,6 +4809,13 @@ static int nv_pm_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long event, void *
     status = nv_set_system_power_state(power_state, nv_procfs_pm_action_depth);
     if (status != NV_OK) {
         nv_printf(NV_DBG_ERRORS, "NVRM: PM %s notifier failed: 0x%x\n", name, status);
+
+        /* A notifier that fails isn't called for PM_POST_HIBERNATION. */
+        if (event == PM_HIBERNATION_PREPARE)
+        {
+            WRITE_ONCE(nv_hibernation_in_progress, NV_FALSE);
+        }
+
         return NOTIFY_BAD;
     }
 
